type, ...])  | Gets the forward, right, and up vector for the agent.\nL28: cite19†`ProfilingSonar` (client, agent_name, agent_type)  | Simulates a multibeam profiling sonar.\nL29: cite20†`RGBCamera` (client, agent_name, agent_type[, ...])  | Captures agent's view.\nL30: cite21†`RangeFinderSensor` (client, agent_name, agent_type)  | Returns distances to nearest collisions in the directions specified by the parameters.\nL31: cite22†`RaycastLidar` (client, agent_name, agent_type)  | Runs Agent's Lidar\nL32: cite23†`RaycastSemanticLidar` (client, agent_name, ...)  | Runs Agent's Semantic Lidar\nL33: cite24†`RotationSensor` (client[, agent_name, ...])  | Gets the rotation of the agent in the world, with rotation XYZ about the fixed frame, in degrees.\nL34: cite25†`SemanticSegmentationCamera` (client, ...[, ...])  | Captures agent's view.\nL35: cite26†`SensorDefinition` (agent_name, agent_type, ...)  | A class for new sensors and their parameters, to be used for adding new sensors.\nL36: cite27†`SensorFactory` ()  | Given a sensor definition, constructs the appropriate HoloOceanSensor object.\nL37: cite28†`SidescanSonar` (client, agent_name, agent_type)  | Simulates a sidescan sonar.\nL38: cite29†`SinglebeamSonar` (client, agent_name, agent_type)  | Simulates an echosounder, which is a sonar sensor with a single cone shaped beam.\nL39: cite30†`VelocitySensor` (client[, agent_name, ...])  | Returns the x, y, and z velocity of the sensor in the global frame.\nL40: cite31†`ViewportCapture` (client, agent_name, agent_type)  | Captures what the viewport is seeing.\nL41: cite32†`WorldNumSensor` (client[, agent_name, ...])  | Returns any numeric value from the world corresponding to a given key.\nL786:   * `AngVelSigma`/`AngVelCov`: Covariance/Std for angular velocity component. Can be scalar, 3-vector or 3x3-matrix. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0 => no noise.\nL787: \nL788:   * `AccelBiasSigma`/`AccelCBiasov`: Covariance/Std for acceleration bias component. Can be scalar, 3-vector or 3x3-matrix. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0 => no noise.\nL789:   * `AngVelBiasSigma`/`AngVelBiasCov`: Covariance/Std for acceleration bias component. Can be scalar, 3-vector or 3x3-matrix. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0 => no noise.\nL790: \nL791:   * `ReturnBias`: Whether the sensor should return the bias along with accel/ang. vel. Defaults to false.\nL792: \nL793: Attributes:\nL794: \nL795: cite69†`data_shape` | The shape of the sensor data\nL796: cite70†`dtype` | The type of data in the sensor\nL797: \nL798: property data_shapecite69† L799: \nL800: \nL801: The shape of the sensor data\nL802: \nL803: Returns:\nL804: \nL805: \nL806: Sensor data shape\nL807: \nL808: Return type:\nL809: `tuple`\nL810: \nL811: property dtypecite70† L812: \nL813: \nL814: The type of data in the sensor\nL815: \nL816: Returns:\nL817: \nL818: \nL819: Type of sensor data\nL820: \nL821: Return type:\nL822: \nL823: \nL824: numpy dtype\nL825: \nL826: class holoocean.sensors.ImagingSonar(client, agent_name, agent_type, name='ImagingSonar', config=None)cite13† L827: \nL828: \nL829: Simulates an imaging sonar. See cite71†Octree Configuration for more on how to configure the octree that is used.\nL830: \nL831: Configuration\nL832: \nL833: The `configuration` block (see cite34†Configuration Block ) accepts any of the options in the following sections.\nL834: \nL835: Basic Configuration\nL836:   * `Azimuth`: Azimuth (side to side) angle visible in degrees, defaults to 120.\nL837: \nL838:   * `Elevation`: Elevation angle (up and down) visible in degrees, defaults to 20.\nL839: \nL840:   * `RangeMin`: Minimum range visible in meters, defaults to 0.1.\nL841: \nL842:   * `RangeMax`: Maximum range visible in meters, defaults to 10.\nL843: \nL844:   * `RangeBins`/`RangeRes`: Number of range bins of resulting image, or resolution (length in meters) of each bin. Set one or the other. Defaults to 512 bins.\nL845:   * `AzimuthBins`/`AzimuthRes`: Number of azimuth bins of resulting image, or resolution (length in degrees) of each bin. Set one or the other. Defaults to 512 bins.\nL846: \nL847: Noise Configuration\nL848: \nL849:   * `AddSigma`/`AddCov`: Additive noise std/covariance from a Rayleigh distribution. Needs to be a float. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0, or off.\nL850: \nL851:   * `MultSigma`/`MultCov`: Multiplication noise std/covariance from a normal distribution. Needs to be a float. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0, or off.\nL852:   * `MultiPath`: Whether to compute multipath or not. Defaults to False.\nL853: \nL854:   * `ClusterSize`: Size of cluster when multipath is enabled. Defaults to 5.\nL855: \nL856:   * `ScaleNoise`: Whether to scale the returned intensities or not. Defaults to False.\nL857: \nL858:   * `AzimuthStreaks`: What sort of azimuth artifacts to introduce. -1 is a removal artifact, 0 is no artifact, and 1 is increased gain artifact. Defaults to 0.\nL859:   * `RangeSigma`: Additive noise std from an exponential distribution that will be added to the range measurements, and the intensities will be scaled by the pdf. Needs to be a float. Defaults to 0, or off.\nL860: \nL861: Advanced Configuration\nL862: \nL863:   * `ShowWarning`: Whether to show on screen warning about sonar computation happening. Defaults to True.\nL864:   * `ElevationBins`/`ElevationRes`: Number of elevation bins used when shadowing is done, or resolution (length in degrees) of each bin. Set one or the other. By default this is computed based on the octree size and the min/max range. Should only be set if shadowing isn’t working.\nL865: \nL866:   * `InitOctreeRange`: Upon startup, all mid-level octrees within this distance of the agent will be created.\nL867: \nL868:   * `ViewRegion`: Turns on green lines to see visible region. Defaults to False.\nL1129: cite83†`data_shape` | The shape of the sensor data\nL1130: cite84†`dtype` | The type of data in the sensor\nL1131: \nL1132: property data_shapecite83† L1133: \nL1134: \nL1135: The shape of the sensor data\nL1136: \nL1137: Returns:\nL1138: \nL1139: \nL1140: Sensor data shape\nL1141: \nL1142: Return type:\nL1143: \nL1144: \nL1145: `tuple`\nL1146: \nL1147: property dtypecite84† L1148: \nL1149: \nL1150: The type of data in the sensor\nL1151: \nL1152: Returns:\nL1153: \nL1154: \nL1155: Type of sensor data\nL1156: \nL1157: Return type:\nL1158: \nL1159: \nL1160: numpy dtype\nL1161: \nL1162: class holoocean.sensors.ProfilingSonar(client, agent_name, agent_type, name='ProfilingSonar', config=None)cite19† L1163: Simulates a multibeam profiling sonar. This is largely based off of the imaging sonar (cite13†`ImagingSonar` ), just with different defaults. See cite71†Octree Configuration for more on how to configure the octree that is used.\nL1164: \nL1165: Configuration\nL1166: \nL1167: The `configuration` block (see cite34†Configuration Block ) accepts any of the options in the following sections.\nL1168: \nL1169: Basic Configuration\nL1170: \nL1171:   * `Azimuth`: Azimuth (side to side) angle visible in degrees, defaults to 120.\nL1172:   * `Elevation`: Elevation angle (up and down) visible in degrees, defaults to 1.\nL1173: \nL1174:   * `RangeMin`: Minimum range visible in meters, defaults to 0.5.\nL1175: \nL1176:   * `RangeMax`: Maximum range visible in meters, defaults to 75.\nL1177: \nL1178:   * `RangeBins`/`RangeRes`: Number of range bins of resulting image, or resolution (length in meters) of each bin. Set one or the other. Defaults to 750 bins.\nL1179:   * `AzimuthBins`/`AzimuthRes`: Number of azimuth bins of resulting image, or resolution (length in degrees) of each bin. Set one or the other. Defaults to 480 bins.\nL1180: \nL1181: Noise Configuration\nL1182: \nL1183:   * `AddSigma`/`AddCov`: Additive noise std/covariance from a Rayleigh distribution. Needs to be a float. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0, or off.\nL1184: \nL1185:   * `MultSigma`/`MultCov`: Multiplication noise std/covariance from a normal distribution. Needs to be a float. Set one or the other. Defaults to 0, or off.\nL1186:   * `MultiPath`: Whether to compute multipath or not. Defaults to False.\nL1187: \nL1188:   * `ClusterSize`: Size of cluster when multipath is enabled. Defaults to 5.\nL1189: \nL1190:   * `ScaleNoise`: Whether to scale the returned intensities or not. Defaults to False.\nL1191: \nL1192:   * `AzimuthStreaks`: What sort of azimuth artifacts to introduce. -1 is a removal artifact, 0 is no artifact, and 1 is increased gain artifact. Defaults to 0.\n"
